      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence supports that the authors address why Twitter predicts language inventories better, though their explanations are partial and framed as hypotheses/observations. The Discussion states Twitter has fewer missing languages (fewer false negatives), and the Population Demographics section notes Twitter better represents North America and Oceania and that common languages like English and Spanish are well represented on Twitter, which can inflate true positive rates. The Discussion also hypothesizes Twitter represents more wealthy populations (matching GDP-weighted populations and urban areas). These together constitute the authors' offered explanations for Twitter's better language-inventory predictions."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 3249.6137999987695
