            ]
          },
          {
            "key": "gdp_weighting_hypothesis",
            "text": "The authors state that Twitter data matches populations better when population numbers are weighted by GDP and worse when weighted by internet-usage statistics, implying that Twitter represents more wealthy populations than web-crawled data, with an alternate interpretation that the Twitter collection is based on urban areas.",
